        Cells that span rows. rowspan="n" makes a cell as tall as n rows and the gaps between them, and the rows
        under it leave its column out: their cells start at the first free columns. Each quarter label spans the
        quarter's four rows, and each note spans two. A note taller than the rows it spans makes the last of them
        grow. The rows a cell spans stay on one page, so a quarter that does not fit moves to the next page whole,
        under the header that the table repeats there, and a year banner, which keeps with the next row, goes with
        the first quarter under it. The grid border has no rule across a spanning cell.
      -->
